/-!
# The functor of quotients is an fpqc sheaf (Stacks 082P)

In Situation 082M — a morphism `f : X ⟶ Y` of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S` and a
quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module `F` — the functor of quotients `Q_{F/X/Y}` of Stacks 082N and its
finite-presentation subfunctor `Q^{fp}_{F/X/Y}` of Stacks 0CZL satisfy the sheaf property for the
fpqc topology.

## Main results

* `QuotientSituation.exists_mem_quotients_quotientPullback_eq`: a family of quotients over the
  members of an fpqc covering `{U i ⟶ T}` of test schemes which agree on the overlaps `U i ×_T U j`
  is the family of pullbacks of a quotient over `T`.
* `QuotientSituation.eq_of_quotientPullback_eq`: a quotient over `T` is determined by its
  pullbacks to the members of an fpqc covering of `T`.
* `QuotientSituation.isSheafFor_quotientsFunctor_of_isFpqcCovering`: the functor of quotients
  `Q_{F/X/Y}` satisfies the sheaf property for fpqc coverings.
* `QuotientSituation.isSheafFor_finitePresentationQuotientsFunctor_of_isFpqcCovering`: so does its
  finite-presentation subfunctor `Q^{fp}_{F/X/Y}`.

## Implementation notes

There is no fpqc topology on the test schemes over an algebraic space here, so, as for
Stacks 08K8, "satisfies the sheaf property for the fpqc topology" is
`CategoryTheory.Presieve.IsSheafFor` for the presieve generated by an arbitrary fpqc covering
family `{U i ⟶ T}` of test schemes over `Y`, the covering condition being the fpqc condition of
Stacks 03MQ for the underlying family of algebraic spaces.

The base changes `{X_{U i} ⟶ X_T}` form an fpqc covering of
`X_T` (Stacks 03MR, `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFpqcCovering_baseChangeMap`), and the fibre
product `X_{U i} ×_{X_T} X_{U j}` maps to the base change of the overlap `U i ×_T U j`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HomSituation.overlapTestComparison`), so a compatible family of
quotients agrees on the fibre products of the covering of `X_T`.  Remark 08IU, in the form of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.descendsQuotientsAlongFpqcCovering_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite'`, then
gives a quasi-coherent quotient `F_T ⟶ Q` restricting to the given ones; its uniqueness is the
injectivity half of 08IU (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.eq_of_quotientRestrictOver_eq`).  `Q` is
flat over `T` because flatness over the base descends along the flat base change
`U i ⟶ T` at every point (the second part of Stacks 05VW,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFlatOverAtPoint_baseChange`, the points of `X_T` being covered by
those of the `X_{U i}`), and in the finitely presented case `Q` is of finite presentation by
Stacks 060V (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.finitePresentationOnSiteDescendsAlongFpqcCovering`).

